fn=fn.replace("    fig.savefig(f'out/charts/{fn}.png'); plt.close(fig); t.to_csv(f'out/charts/{fn}.csv')\n    print(fn); print(t.round(3).to_string())\n","    plt.show(); print(t.round(3))\n")
blocks=re.split(r"\n# (\d) (\w+)\n",ch[ch.index("def tab(key)"):ch.index("print('pre'")])
md("# 02 — Features · Crowdfund Compass (Group 11)\nGoal: turn the merged table into 34 features in 6 groups, using only what a founder knows **before launch**, and look at each group's raw relation to success.\n\nWorkflow: 1) Setup → 2) Import → 3) Build features → 4) Check the before-launch rule → 5) Signal per feature → 6) One chart per group → 7) Conclusions.\n\n*AI use: code written with Claude (Fable 5.2), 16.11.2026; reviewed by the team.*")
md("## 1) Setup\n`features.py` is our shared feature module (the app will use the same file). Put it in the same Drive folder as this notebook.")
code("import sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score\n!pip -q install vaderSentiment        # sentiment word list (beyond class)\n\n# from google.colab import drive; drive.mount('/content/drive')\nproject = 'drive/My Drive/crowdfund_compass'      # folder with features.py\npath = 'drive/My Drive/ks_scrapes/merged_v2'      # folder with kickstarter_merged_v2_part1..8.parquet\nsys.path.insert(0, project)\nimport features as F")
md("## 2) Import the data")
code("raw = F.load_merged(path)\nprint(len(raw), 'projects')")
md("## 3) Build the features\nOne call builds everything (about 2 minutes). What it does, group by group:\n- **Ambition:** goal in USD, goal compared with the category's median goal, goal per day, duration, round-number goal.\n- **Timing:** launch month and weekday, campaign runs over Christmas, preparation time.\n- **Pitch:** length of title and blurb, digits/symbols/capitals in the title, readability, sentiment, four keyword flags.\n- **Founder:** number and success of the creator's earlier campaigns.\n- **Presentation:** video, pre-launch page (known only for recent projects; used in the modern model only).\n- **Market:** category, country, the category's recent funding rate, trend and size.\n\nDropped after this notebook's first run (16.11): three crowding features, city size and title capitalisation (it made the Pitch score depend on Title Case). Inside a category they had no signal (AUC 0.49–0.51), and crowding mostly reflected which categories the scraper covers well.\n\nHistory rule: category norms use campaigns that ended in the 12 months before the first day of the launch month; creator history uses only campaigns that ended before the launch itself.")
code("X, tables = F.build_features(raw)\nfeatures = [f for group in F.GROUPS.values() for f in group]\nprint(len(features), 'features in', len(F.GROUPS), 'groups')\nfor group, cols in F.GROUPS.items():\n    print(f'{group:13s}', cols)")
md("## 4) Check the before-launch rule\nWe recompute the creator history for 200 random projects in a slow, obvious way and compare it with the module. Any mismatch would mean a bug or a leak.")
code("hist = raw[raw.state.isin(['successful', 'failed', 'canceled', 'suspended']) & (raw.launched_at > 1.2e9)]\nmismatch = 0\nfor r in X[X.creator_prior_n > 0].sample(200, random_state=1).itertuples():\n    earlier = hist[(hist.creator_id == r.creator_id) & (hist.deadline < r.launched_at)]   # ended BEFORE this launch\n    mismatch += (len(earlier) != r.creator_prior_n) or ((earlier.state == 'successful').sum() != r.creator_prior_funded)\nprint('mismatches:', mismatch, 'of 200')")
md("## 5) Signal per feature\nFor launches 2023–2024 (the years where every feature is known) we measure how well each feature **alone** separates funded from failed campaigns. AUC 0.5 = no signal; further from 0.5 = stronger. Because our sample over-represents funded campaigns differently in each category, we also compute the AUC **inside each parent category** and **inside each category**, then average.")
code("E = X[X.launch_year.isin([2023, 2024]) & X.has_video.notna()].copy()\nprint(len(E), 'campaigns | funded in sample:', round(E.success.mean(), 3))\n\ndef auc_within(df, feature, by=None):\n    if by is None:\n        v = df[[feature, 'success']].dropna()\n        return roc_auc_score(v.success, v[feature])\n    total = weight = 0\n    for _, g in df.groupby(by):\n        v = g[[feature, 'success']].dropna()\n        if v.success.nunique() == 2 and v[feature].nunique() > 1:\n            total += roc_auc_score(v.success, v[feature]) * len(v); weight += len(v)\n    return total / weight\n\nrows = []\nfor group, cols in F.GROUPS.items():\n    for f in cols:\n        if f in ('cat_id', 'parent_category', 'country'): continue      # labels, not numbers\n        rows.append((group, f, auc_within(E, f), auc_within(E, f, 'parent_category'), auc_within(E, f, 'cat_id')))\nsignal = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=['group', 'feature', 'AUC overall', 'AUC within parent', 'AUC within category']).round(3)\nsignal['strength'] = (signal['AUC within category'] - 0.5).abs()\nprint(signal.sort_values(['group', 'strength'], ascending=[True, False]).to_string(index=False))")
md("**Interpretation:** the creator's track record, the goal, the preparation time and the pre-launch page carry signal even inside a category. The market features (category funding rate and size) look strongest overall but lose most of their signal inside a category: part of what they measure is which categories the scraper covers well, not real odds.")
md("## 6) One chart per feature group\nEach chart shows the share of campaigns funded **in our sample** (launches 2023–2024). These are associations, not causes.")
code("AVG = E.success.mean(); N = len(E)\nACC, GREY, INK, MUTE = '#0F7C82', '#C5CAD3', '#1B2A41', '#5B6676'\nSUB = f'Share of campaigns funded, in our sample. Finished Kickstarter campaigns launched 2023–2024 (n = {N:,}).'\nNOTE = 'Sample rates are higher than real Kickstarter rates (many failed campaigns are missing). Association, not cause.'\n"+fn+"def tab(key): return E.groupby(key, observed=True).success.agg(n='size', funded='mean')")
for i in range(1,len(blocks),3):
    md(f"### 6.{blocks[i]} {blocks[i+1]}")
    code(blocks[i+2].strip())
md("## 7) Conclusions\n1. 34 features in 6 groups (the final model uses 32: it drops the three category norms after the test in notebook 03 and adds a text score built there), all computed from information available before launch; the history check finds no mismatch.\n2. Strongest signals inside a category: creator track record, goal size, preparation time, pre-launch page.\n3. Video alone and most pitch-wording features are weak on their own; TF-IDF in the model notebook will test the text properly.\n4. Market features are partly an artefact of scraper coverage and must be read with care.\n5. All rates here are sample rates: too high in absolute terms.")
